"desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 4.62"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":107.67,"default_fair_val":107.67,"premium_pct":147.7,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":35.7,"pe_forward":31.4,"pb_trailing":4.6,"pb_forward":4.1,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":9.2,"fcf_to_ev":2.82,"fcf_to_mcap":2.71,"liab_to_assets":17.2,"cash_to_assets":24.5,"current_ratio":4.62,"roe":12.8,"roa":10.6,"moat":{"ticker":"TWLO","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Twilio 的品牌在開發者社群中享有盛譽，其平台被視為可靠且功能強大的通訊 API 解決方案。然而，其定價權相對有限，因為市場上存在其他競爭者提供類似的服務，且客戶對價格敏感度較高。雖然其品牌有助於吸引新客戶，但要將品牌優勢轉化為顯著的定價權仍有挑戰，尤其是在面對價格競爭時。","comment_en":"Twilio commands strong brand recognition within the developer community, positioning its platform as a reliable and powerful communication API solution. However, its pricing power is relatively limited due to the presence of competitors offering similar services and customer price sensitivity. While the brand helps attract new customers, translating this into significant pricing power remains a challenge, especially when facing price competition."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Twilio 的業務模式主要依賴軟體和服務，而非依賴受專利保護的獨特技術。雖然其平台可能包含一些專利技術，但這些專利並非其核心競爭壁壘。該行業的監管環境相對寬鬆，沒有顯著的監管壁壘可以阻止新進入者。因此，專利和監管在 Twilio 的護城河中扮演的角色非常有限。","comment_en":"Twilio's business model relies heavily on software and services rather than unique, patent-protected technology. While its platform may incorporate some patented technologies, these patents do not form its core competitive moat. The industry's regulatory environment is relatively permissive, with no significant regulatory barriers preventing new entrants. Consequently, patents and regulations play a very limited role in Twilio's moat."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Twilio 的客戶，特別是那些深度整合其 API 的企業，面臨較高的轉換成本。將 Twilio 的通訊服務從其應用程式和工作流程中移除，需要大量的工程資源、重新開發和測試。這種整合的深度，加上對平台穩定性和功能的依賴，為 Twilio 創造了顯著的客戶黏性，使其成為客戶難以輕易替換的選擇。","comment_en":"Twilio's customers, especially those with deep integration of its APIs into their applications and workflows, face substantial switching costs. Migrating away from Twilio's communication services requires significant engineering effort, redevelopment, and testing. This depth of integration, coupled with reliance on the platform's stability and functionality, creates considerable customer stickiness, making it difficult for clients to switch easily."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Twilio 的網絡效應相對有限。雖然其平台連接了開發者和企業，但這種連接並未形成強烈的雙邊網絡效應，即用戶越多並不必然導致服務價值指數級增長。開發者生態系統的存在有助於吸引更多開發者，但這更多是基於平台的實用性和工具集，而非傳統意義上的網絡效應壁壘。","comment_en":"Twilio's network effects are relatively limited. While its platform connects developers and businesses, this connection does not create strong two-sided network effects where more users lead to an exponential increase in service value. The existence of a developer ecosystem helps attract more developers, but this is more based on the platform's utility and toolset rather than traditional network effect barriers."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Twilio 作為領先的雲通訊平台，透過其龐大的客戶基礎和高交易量，實現了顯著的規模經濟。這使其能夠與電信營運商協商更優惠的價格，並優化基礎設施成本。這種成本優勢使其在價格上比小型競爭者更具競爭力，並能持續投資於平台擴張和創新，鞏固其市場地位。","comment_en":"As a leading cloud communications platform, Twilio benefits from significant economies of scale due to its vast customer base and high transaction volumes. This allows it to negotiate favorable rates with telecom carriers and optimize infrastructure costs. This cost advantage makes it more competitive on price than smaller rivals and enables continued investment in platform expansion and innovation, solidifying its market position."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Twilio 的業務本質上是全球性的軟體服務，不依賴於特定的地理位置或獨特的實體資產。其數據中心和基礎設施遍布全球，以提供服務，但這些並非構成獨特的地理壁壘。其競爭優勢來自於技術、客戶關係和規模，而非地理位置的稀缺性。","comment_en":"Twilio's business is inherently a global software service, not reliant on specific geographic locations or unique physical assets. Its data centers and infrastructure are distributed globally to provide service, but these do not constitute unique geographical barriers. Its competitive advantages stem from technology, customer relationships, and scale, not from geographical scarcity."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Twilio 在營運效率方面表現出色，其雲原生架構和自動化流程使其能夠高效地處理海量通訊請求。透過持續優化基礎設施和軟體堆疊，Twilio 能夠維持高可用性和低延遲，同時控制成本。這種營運上的精實，是其能夠提供具競爭力價格和可靠服務的關鍵。","comment_en":"Twilio demonstrates strong operational efficiency, with its cloud-native architecture and automated processes enabling it to handle massive volumes of communication requests effectively. By continuously optimizing its infrastructure and software stack, Twilio maintains high availability and low latency while controlling costs. This operational leaness is key to its ability to offer competitive pricing and reliable services."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Twilio 在過去展現了積極的資本配置策略，透過策略性收購擴展其產品組合和市場覆蓋範圍，例如收購 SendGrid。同時，公司也持續投資於研發以維持技術領先地位。儘管有時會進行較大的收購，但整體而言，其資本配置旨在推動長期成長和鞏固市場領導地位。","comment_en":"Twilio has historically pursued an active capital allocation strategy, expanding its product portfolio and market reach through strategic acquisitions, such as SendGrid. The company also consistently invests in R&D to maintain its technological edge. While acquisitions have sometimes been substantial, its capital allocation generally aims to drive long-term growth and solidify its market leadership."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Twilio 的客戶留存率相對較高，這得益於其平台的高度整合性和較高的轉換成本。一旦客戶將其核心通訊功能建立在 Twilio 平台上，遷移到其他供應商的成本和複雜性就會很高。此外，Twilio 持續推出新功能和服務，以滿足客戶不斷變化的需求，進一步增強客戶忠誠度。","comment_en":"Twilio enjoys relatively high customer retention, attributed to the deep integration of its platform and the associated switching costs. Once customers build their core communication functionalities on Twilio, the cost and complexity of migrating to another provider become significant. Furthermore, Twilio continuously introduces new features and services to meet evolving customer needs, further enhancing loyalty."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Twilio 的業務模式具有一定的持久性，因為企業對可靠、可擴展的雲通訊解決方案的需求持續增長。然而，科技行業的快速變化和潛在的新進入者帶來了挑戰。其核心競爭力在於持續創新和適應市場變化，而非某種不可動搖的壟斷地位。其持久性取決於能否維持技術領先和客戶關係。","comment_en":"Twilio's business model possesses a degree of durability, as the demand for reliable, scalable cloud communication solutions continues to grow. However, the rapid pace of change in the tech industry and potential new entrants pose challenges. Its core strength lies in continuous innovation and adaptation rather than an unshakeable monopoly. Its durability depends on maintaining technological leadership and customer relationships."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Twilio 的護城河主要建立在較高的客戶轉換成本（M3）和顯著的規模經濟（M5）之上，使其在雲通訊領域佔據領先地位。其品牌（M1）在開發者社群中具有一定影響力，但定價權有限。網絡效應（M4）相對薄弱，專利和監管（M2）壁壘幾乎不存在。營運效率（M7）和資本配置（M8）為其成長提供了支持，客戶留存（M9）也相對穩固。總體而言，Twilio 類似於一個「收費橋」模式，客戶因整合的深度而難以離開，但其護城河並非堅不可摧，面臨持續的技術和市場競爭壓力。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Twilio's moat is primarily built upon high switching costs (M3) and significant economies of scale (M5), establishing its leadership in cloud communications. Its brand (M1) holds sway in the developer community but offers limited pricing power. Network effects (M4) are relatively weak, and patent/regulatory barriers (M2) are minimal. Operational efficiency (M7) and capital allocation (M8) support its growth, with customer retention (M9) being relatively strong. Overall, Twilio operates somewhat like a 'toll bridge,' where customers are locked in due to deep integration, but its moat is not impregnable, facing continuous technological and market competition.","evidenceHash":"fe3b0eabf7408293b2d6885cc95c44b615096a462595b40c807ce969983c5681","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"1092a0229639d277c449cecce416bdf31fd6bbce7da5cf12c89130cd0b9cff11"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"1092a0229639d277c449cecce416bdf31fd6bbce7da5cf12c89130cd0b9cff11"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TWLO.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TWLO.png","website":"https://www.twilio.com","ceo":"Khozema Z. Shipchandler","full_time_employees":"5587","description":"Twilio Inc. offers a comprehensive cloud-based communications platform, empowering developers to build, scale, and manage customer engagement features directly within their software applications across both U.S. and international markets. Central to its customer engagement solution is a robust suite of application programming interfaces (APIs). These APIs streamline the complex communication logic required for various customer interactions and enable developers to seamlessly integrate voice, messaging, video, and email functionalities into their applications. Established in 2008, Twilio's corporate headquarters are located in San Francisco, California.","description_en":"Twilio Inc. offers a comprehensive cloud-based communications platform, empowering developers to build, scale, and manage customer engagement features directly within their software applications across both U.S. and international markets. Central to its customer engagement solution is a robust suite of application programming interfaces (APIs). These APIs streamline the complex communication logic required for various customer interactions and enable developers to seamlessly integrate voice, messaging, video, and email functionalities into their applications. Established in 2008, Twilio's corporate headquarters are located in San Francisco, California.","description_zh":"**Twilio Inc. (TWLO) 業務營運概述**\n\nTwilio Inc. 是一家領先的雲端通訊平台供應商，致力於賦能開發者在其軟體應用程式中，直接建構、擴展及管理客戶互動功能，服務範圍涵蓋美國及國際市場。\n\n其核心產品為一套強大的應用程式介面 (APIs)，這是客戶互動解決方案的基石。這些 APIs 極大簡化了各種客戶互動所需的複雜通訊邏輯，讓開發者能夠無縫地將語音、簡訊 (SMS)、視訊及電子郵件等功能整合至其應用程式中。\n\nTwilio 的營運模式著重於提供彈性且可擴展的開發者工具，讓企業能夠以程式化的方式，客製化並優化其與客戶的溝通管道。透過其平台，企業得以提升客戶體驗、自動化溝通流程並降低營運成本。公司成立於 2008 年，總部位於美國加州舊金山。","address":"101 Spear Street","city":"San Francisco","state":"CA","zip":"94105","country":"US","phone":"415 390 2337","full_address":"101 Spear Street, San Francisco, CA 94105, US","range_52w":"105-308.4","year_high":308.4,"year_low":105,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":105,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-07","name":"Shipchandler Khozema","title":"director, officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":1934,"price":288.02,"total_val":0.56},{"date":"2026-10-07","name":"Shipchandler Khozema","title":"director, officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":1900,"price":289.13,"total_val":0.55},{"date":"2026-10-07","name":"Shipchandler Khozema","title":"director, officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":5156,"price":290.24,"total_val":1.5},{"date":"2026-10-07","name":"Shipchandler Khozema","title":"director, officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":501,"price":291.47,"total_val":0.15},{"date":"2026-10-07","name":"Shipchandler Khozema","title":"director, officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":800,"price":292.33,"total_val":0.23},{"date":"2026-10-07","name":"Shipchandler Khozema","title":"director, officer: Chief Ex